    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "U. S. S. FOX\nDestroyer No. 234\nGreetings on her 15th Birthday\nCommissioned May 17, 1920\nBuilt by New York Ship Bldg. Co.\nArmaments-Four five-inch 51 caliber\nguns; one three-inch 23 caliber anti-air-\ncraft gun; four twenty-one inch triple\ntorpedo tubes on deck.\nNamed in memory of\nHon. Gustavus Vasa Fox,\nAssistant Secretary of the Navy, August 1,\n1861, to close the Civil War. Served\nduring the Mexican War as a Lieut. in\nthe Navy and, at the commencement of\nthe Civil War, volunteered for service\nand was given a temporary appointment\nin the Navy after which he was made\nAsst. Sec'y. In 1886 he was sent on a\nspecial mission to Russia on board the\nmonitor Miantonomoh, which was the\nfirst vessel of this class to cross\nAtlantic.\nSecond vessel so called. First was Tor-\npedo Boat No. 13.\nS.\nS.\nMAY\n17.\nP.M.\n1935\n+\nLAT. 21\nLONG.\n1\nRANKLI\nWILLIAM FOSTER RICE, JR.\n3515 - 34TH ST.\nLONG ISLAND CITY, N.Y.",
      "3 r B- BBT.\n164-08 yU\nTHEO. HARRINGTON\n2057 So 29TH ST..\nMILVAUKEE,\n2008,075.078a\nB II",
      "(1)TTTLE\nRACIFIC ISLANDS - WAKE\n(2)CODE\n(3)* ONLY 632 (4)# CONTI\n(2)\n(5) ALPHA\n(6)# AFTER ALPHA\n(7)# AFT ALPHA CONT'D\n(B)D ESCRIPTION \"USS\n\"USS Fox 5/11/35. LAT 21.59 N\nLONG\n164.08 W. \" PME ON C\n$#\nOVR\n(9)VALUE\n(OTHERS\n4\n5\nPDC ?\nCONTENTS?"
